      "id": 1,
      "text": "Port Byron takes its name from the English poet Lord Byron, a favorite of founder Nathaniel Belcher.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rivervalleylibrary.org/historical-society",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1861, two railroads—Warsaw, Rock Island & Galena and Sterling Rock Island—made Port Byron a terminal stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rivervalleylibrary.org/historical-society",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The River Valley Library’s second floor holds the Port Byron Historical Society archives, safeguarding the village’s stories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rivervalleylibrary.org/historical-society",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Founded in 1997, the Port Byron Historical Society meets monthly at the library to research and share local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
